IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc31-forms-statements.l4 -- Forms 34.1, 34.2, 34.3 and 48.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the Statement on
-- Restitution, the Victim Impact Statement, the Community Impact Statement and the Victim Impact Statement -- Not Criminally Responsible.
-- Layer 1: the law as the Forms state it, from the text alone, from no one's point of view. (Written by work/gen-statements.py, which keeps
-- the three statement Forms in step; the quotations are copied by srcrefs.py from the text.)
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read a result (NOTES.md): MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the Form says the statement may include the item. JUST FALSE: the Form says no
-- in its own words ("Your statement must not include"; "this is not an application"; "not required"). NOTHING: not covered (the Form lists
-- examples without closing the list; the court-approval exception once met, fork F8). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The "open-textured" judgment of the item's kind ("not relevant to the harm or loss", "unproven") is a plain input: the caller says which
-- kind the content is.

§ `Form 34.1 (Subsection 737.1(4)) -- Statement on Restitution`

-- src:18652 | FORM 34.1 (Subsection 737.1(4)) Statement on Restitution
-- src:18653 | Canada,
-- src:18654 | Province of ,
-- src:18655 | (territorial division).
-- src:18656 | To the court that is sentencing (name the offender) who was convicted, or was discharged under section 730 of the Criminal Code, of an offence under that Act.
-- src:18657 | I, (name of declarant), declare that (check the appropriate box):
-- src:18658 | [ ] (i) I am not seeking restitution for the losses and damages I suffered as the result of the commission of the offence.
-- src:18659 | [ ] (ii) I am seeking restitution in the amount of $ for the following losses and damages I suffered as the result of the commission of the offence.
-- src:18660 | I declare that I have suffered the following losses and damages as the result of the commission of the offence:
-- src:18661 | (Complete the following table if seeking restitution.)
-- src:18662 | Description(describe each loss and damage) | Amount of loss and damage(state the amount of each loss and damage)
-- src:18663 | 1.
-- src:18664 | 2.
-- src:18665 | 3.
-- src:18666 | 4.
-- src:18667 | I understand that the amount of my losses and damages must be readily ascertainable by the court. For that purpose, I am responsible for providing the court with all necessary documents, including bills, receipts and estimates, in support of my claim for restitution.
-- src:18668 | Dated this day of 20, at .
-- src:18669 | Signature of declarant
@ref Form 34.1 (Subsection 737.1(4)) (src:18652-18669)
GIVEN `the court is sentencing the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender was convicted of an offence under the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender was discharged under section 730 of the Criminal Code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34.1 the statement is addressed to a court sentencing an offender convicted or discharged under section 730` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is sentencing the offender`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the court that is sentencing (name the offender)"
        IF `the offender was convicted of an offence under the Criminal Code` OR `the offender was discharged under section 730 of the Criminal Code`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who was convicted, or was discharged under section 730 of the Criminal Code, of an offence under that Act"

-- "I understand that the amount of my losses and damages must be readily ascertainable by the court."
@ref Form 34.1 (Subsection 737.1(4)) (src:18667)
GIVEN `the amount of the loss or damage is readily ascertainable by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34.1 the loss may be claimed as restitution` MEANS
    IF `the amount of the loss or damage is readily ascertainable by the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amount of my losses and damages must be readily ascertainable by the court"

-- "For that purpose, I am responsible for providing the court with all necessary documents, including bills, receipts and estimates, in support of my claim for restitution."
@ref Form 34.1 (Subsection 737.1(4)) (src:18667)
GIVEN `the person is the declarant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declarant is seeking restitution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34.1 the declarant is responsible for providing the documents` MEANS
    IF `the person is the declarant` AND `the declarant is seeking restitution`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "I am responsible for providing the court with all necessary documents ... in support of my claim for restitution": the responsibility is the declarant's, for a claim

§ `Form 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) -- Victim Impact Statement`

-- src:18671 | FORM 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) Victim Impact Statement
-- src:18672 | This form may be used to provide a description of the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by you as the result of the commission of an offence, as well as a description of the impact of the offence on you. You may attach additional pages if you need more space.
-- src:18673 | Your statement must not include
-- src:18674 | • any statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss you suffered;
-- src:18675 | • any unproven allegations;
-- src:18676 | • any comments about any offence for which the offender was not convicted;
-- src:18677 | • any complaint about any individual, other than the offender, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence; or
-- src:18678 | • except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence.
-- src:18679 | You may present a detailed account of the impact the offence has had on your life. The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement. You are not required to include all of this information.
-- src:18680 | Emotional impact
-- src:18681 | Describe how the offence has affected you emotionally. For example, think of
-- src:18682 | • your lifestyle and activities;
-- src:18683 | • your relationships with others such as your spouse, family and friends;
-- src:18684 | • your ability to work, attend school or study; and
-- src:18685 | • your feelings, emotions and reactions as they relate to the offence.
-- src:18686 | Physical impact
-- src:18687 | Describe how the offence has affected you physically. For example, think of
-- src:18688 | • ongoing physical pain, discomfort, illness, scarring, disfigurement or physical limitation;
-- src:18689 | • hospitalization or surgery you have had because of the offence;
-- src:18690 | • treatment, physiotherapy or medication you have been prescribed;
-- src:18691 | • the need for any further treatment or the expectation that you will receive further treatment; and
-- src:18692 | • any permanent or long-term disability.
-- src:18693 | Economic impact
-- src:18694 | Describe how the offence has affected you financially. For example, think of
-- src:18695 | • the value of any property that was lost or damaged and the cost of repairs or replacement;
-- src:18696 | • any financial loss due to missed time from work;
-- src:18697 | • the cost of any medical expenses, therapy or counselling;
-- src:18698 | • any costs or losses that are not covered by insurance.
-- src:18699 | Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution.
-- src:18700 | Fears for security
-- src:18701 | Describe any fears you have for your security or that of your family and friends. For example, think of
-- src:18702 | • concerns with respect to contact with the offender; and
-- src:18703 | • concerns with respect to contact between the offender and members of your family or close friends.
-- src:18704 | Drawing, poem or letter
-- src:18705 | You may use this space to draw a picture or write a poem or letter if it will help you express the impact that the offence has had on you.
-- src:18706 | □ I would like to present my statement in court.
-- src:18707 | □ I would like to receive information respecting the sentence imposed on the offender and its administration.
-- src:18708 | To the best of my knowledge, the information contained in this statement is true.
-- src:18709 | Dated this day of 20, at .
-- src:18710 | Signature of declarant
-- src:18711 | If you completed this statement on behalf of the victim, please indicate the reasons why you did so and the nature of your relationship with the victim.
-- src:18712 | Dated this day of 20, at .
-- src:18713 | Signature of declarant
@ref Form 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) (src:18671-18713)
DECLARE `form 34.2 the kind of content` IS ONE OF
    `form 34.2 emotional impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18680)
    `form 34.2 physical impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18686)
    `form 34.2 economic impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18693)
    `form 34.2 fears for security`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18700)
    `form 34.2 a drawing, poem or letter`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18704)
    `form 34.2 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18674)
    `form 34.2 an unproven allegation`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18675)
    `form 34.2 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18676)
    `form 34.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18677)
    `form 34.2 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18678)
    `form 34.2 any other content`

-- The statement the victim makes about the harm the offence has done: the Form says what it must not include and gives examples of what it may.
-- The court-approval exception (fork F8): once the approval of the court is given, the Form is silent on whether the opinion or recommendation may be included, so NOTHING.
@ref Form 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) (src:18671-18679)
GIVEN content IS A `form 34.2 the kind of content`
      `the court has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34.2 the statement may include the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER content
    WHEN `form 34.2 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss you suffered"
    WHEN `form 34.2 an unproven allegation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any unproven allegations"
    WHEN `form 34.2 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any comments about any offence for which the offender was not convicted"
    WHEN `form 34.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any complaint about any individual, other than the offender, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
    WHEN `form 34.2 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence` THEN
        IF `the court has approved`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence": with approval the Form is silent (fork F8)
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence"
    WHEN `form 34.2 emotional impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.2 physical impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.2 economic impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.2 fears for security` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.2 a drawing, poem or letter` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement": the sections are examples of information the declarant "may wish to include", and the list of examples is not closed

@ref Form 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) (src:18699)
`form 34.2 this is an application for compensation or restitution` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution"

@ref Form 34.2 (Subsection 722(4)) (src:18679)
`form 34.2 the declarant is required to include all the examples` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You are not required to include all of this information"

§ `Form 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) -- Community Impact Statement`

-- src:18715 | FORM 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) Community Impact Statement
-- src:18716 | This form may be used to provide a description of the harm or loss suffered by a community as the result of the commission of an offence, as well as a description of the impact of the offence on the community. You may attach additional pages if you need more space.
-- src:18717 | Your statement must not include
-- src:18718 | • any statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by the community;
-- src:18719 | • any unproven allegations;
-- src:18720 | • any comments about any offence for which the offender was not convicted;
-- src:18721 | • any complaint about any individual, other than the offender, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence; or
-- src:18722 | • except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence.
-- src:18723 | Name of community on whose behalf the statement is made:
-- src:18724 | Explain how the statement reflects this community’s views:
-- src:18725 | You may present a detailed account of the impact the offence has had on the community. The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement. You are not required to include all of this information.
-- src:18726 | Emotional impact
-- src:18727 | Describe how the offence has affected community members emotionally. For example, think of
-- src:18728 | • community members’ lifestyles and activities;
-- src:18729 | • community members’ relationships with others in the community and outside it;
-- src:18730 | • community members’ ability to work, attend school or study;
-- src:18731 | • community members’ feelings, emotions and reactions as they relate to the offence; and
-- src:18732 | • the community’s sense of belonging to the region.
-- src:18733 | Physical impact
-- src:18734 | Describe how the offence has affected community members physically. For example, think of
-- src:18735 | • the ability of community members to access services; and
-- src:18736 | • changes in transportation and routes taken to and from school, work, shopping, etc.
-- src:18737 | Economic impact
-- src:18738 | Describe how the offence has affected the community financially. For example, think of
-- src:18739 | • any reduction in the number of visitors or tourists to the region;
-- src:18740 | • the value of any property that was lost or damaged and the cost of repairs or replacement; and
-- src:18741 | • any costs or losses that are not covered by insurance.
-- src:18742 | Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution.
-- src:18743 | Fears for security
-- src:18744 | Describe any fears that community members have for their security or that of their family and friends. For example, think of concerns with respect to contact with the offender.
-- src:18745 | Drawing, poem or letter
-- src:18746 | You may use this space to draw a picture or write a poem or letter if it will help you express the impact that the offence has had on the community.
-- src:18747 |  I would like to present this statement in court.
-- src:18748 | To the best of my knowledge, the information contained in this statement is true.
-- src:18749 | Dated this day of 20, at .
-- src:18750 | Signature of declarant
@ref Form 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) (src:18715-18750)
DECLARE `form 34.3 the kind of content` IS ONE OF
    `form 34.3 emotional impact on community members`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18726)
    `form 34.3 physical impact on community members`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18733)
    `form 34.3 economic impact on the community`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18737)
    `form 34.3 fears of community members for their security`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18743)
    `form 34.3 a drawing, poem or letter`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18745)
    `form 34.3 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by the community`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18718)
    `form 34.3 an unproven allegation`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18719)
    `form 34.3 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18720)
    `form 34.3 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18721)
    `form 34.3 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18722)
    `form 34.3 any other content`

-- The statement made on behalf of a community about the harm the offence has done to it.
-- The court-approval exception (fork F8): once the approval of the court is given, the Form is silent on whether the opinion or recommendation may be included, so NOTHING.
@ref Form 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) (src:18715-18725)
GIVEN content IS A `form 34.3 the kind of content`
      `the court has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34.3 the statement may include the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER content
    WHEN `form 34.3 a statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by the community` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any statement about the offence or the offender that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by the community"
    WHEN `form 34.3 an unproven allegation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any unproven allegations"
    WHEN `form 34.3 a comment about an offence for which the offender was not convicted` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any comments about any offence for which the offender was not convicted"
    WHEN `form 34.3 a complaint about an individual, other than the offender, involved in the investigation or prosecution` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any complaint about any individual, other than the offender, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
    WHEN `form 34.3 an opinion or recommendation about the sentence` THEN
        IF `the court has approved`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence": with approval the Form is silent (fork F8)
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the court’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the sentence"
    WHEN `form 34.3 emotional impact on community members` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.3 physical impact on community members` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.3 economic impact on the community` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.3 fears of community members for their security` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 34.3 a drawing, poem or letter` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement": the sections are examples of information the declarant "may wish to include", and the list of examples is not closed

@ref Form 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) (src:18742)
`form 34.3 this is an application for compensation or restitution` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution"

@ref Form 34.3 (Subsection 722.2(2)) (src:18725)
`form 34.3 the declarant is required to include all the examples` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You are not required to include all of this information"

§ `Form 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) -- Victim Impact Statement -- Not Criminally Responsible`

-- src:18907 | FORM 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) Victim Impact Statement — Not Criminally Responsible
-- src:18908 | This form may be used to provide a description of the physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss suffered by you arising from the conduct for which the accused person was found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, as well as a description of the impact that the conduct has had on you. You may attach additional pages if you need more space.
-- src:18909 | Your statement must not include
-- src:18910 | • any statement about the conduct of the accused that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by you;
-- src:18911 | • any unproven allegations;
-- src:18912 | • any comments about any conduct for which the accused was not found not criminally responsible;
-- src:18913 | • any complaint about any individual, other than the accused, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence; or
-- src:18914 | • except with the court’s or Review Board’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the disposition.
-- src:18915 | The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement. You are not required to include all of this information.
-- src:18916 | Emotional impact
-- src:18917 | Describe how the accused’s conduct has affected you emotionally. For example, think of
-- src:18918 | • your lifestyle and activities;
-- src:18919 | • your relationships with others such as your spouse, family and friends;
-- src:18920 | • your ability to work, attend school or study; and
-- src:18921 | • your feelings, emotions and reactions as these relate to the conduct.
-- src:18922 | Physical impact
-- src:18923 | Describe how the accused’s conduct has affected you physically. For example, think of
-- src:18924 | • ongoing physical pain, discomfort, illness, scarring, disfigurement or physical limitation;
-- src:18925 | • hospitalization or surgery you have had because of the conduct of the accused;
-- src:18926 | • treatment, physiotherapy or medication you have been prescribed;
-- src:18927 | • the need for any further treatment or the expectation that you will receive further treatment; and
-- src:18928 | • any permanent or long-term disability.
-- src:18929 | Economic impact
-- src:18930 | Describe how the accused’s conduct has affected you financially. For example, think of
-- src:18931 | • the value of any property that was lost or damaged and the cost of repairs or replacement;
-- src:18932 | • any financial loss due to missed time from work;
-- src:18933 | • the cost of any medical expenses, therapy or counselling; and
-- src:18934 | • any costs or losses that are not covered by insurance.
-- src:18935 | Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution.
-- src:18936 | Fears for security
-- src:18937 | Describe any fears you have for your security or that of your family and friends. For example, think of
-- src:18938 | • concerns with respect to contact with the accused; and
-- src:18939 | • concerns with respect to contact between the accused and members of your family or close friends.
-- src:18940 | Drawing, poem or letter
-- src:18941 | You may use this space to draw a picture or write a poem or letter if it will help you express the impact that the accused’s conduct has had on you.
-- src:18942 | □ I would like to read or present my statement (in court or before the Review Board).
-- src:18943 | □ I would like to receive information respecting any hearings held to make or review a disposition in respect of the accused.
-- src:18944 | □ I would like to receive information respecting any disposition made in respect of the accused.
-- src:18945 | □ If the accused is discharged absolutely or conditionally, I would like to receive notice of that discharge and of the accused’s intended place of residence.
-- src:18946 | To the best of my knowledge, the information contained in this statement is true.
-- src:18947 | Dated this day of 20, at .
-- src:18948 | Signature of declarant
@ref Form 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) (src:18907-18948)
DECLARE `form 48.2 the kind of content` IS ONE OF
    `form 48.2 emotional impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18916)
    `form 48.2 physical impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18922)
    `form 48.2 economic impact`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18929)
    `form 48.2 fears for security`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18936)
    `form 48.2 a drawing, poem or letter`   -- an example the Form gives (line 18940)
    `form 48.2 a statement about the conduct of the accused that is not relevant to the harm or loss`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18910)
    `form 48.2 an unproven allegation`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18911)
    `form 48.2 a comment about conduct for which the accused was not found not criminally responsible`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18912)
    `form 48.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the accused, involved in the investigation or prosecution`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18913)
    `form 48.2 an opinion or recommendation about the disposition`   -- "Your statement must not include" (line 18914)
    `form 48.2 any other content`

-- The statement the victim makes about the harm the conduct of the accused, found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, has done.
-- The court-approval exception (fork F8): once the approval of the court or the Review Board is given, the Form is silent on whether the opinion or recommendation may be included, so NOTHING.
@ref Form 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) (src:18907-18915)
GIVEN content IS A `form 48.2 the kind of content`
      `the court or the Review Board has approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 48.2 the statement may include the item` MEANS
    CONSIDER content
    WHEN `form 48.2 a statement about the conduct of the accused that is not relevant to the harm or loss` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any statement about the conduct of the accused that is not relevant to the harm or loss suffered by you"
    WHEN `form 48.2 an unproven allegation` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any unproven allegations"
    WHEN `form 48.2 a comment about conduct for which the accused was not found not criminally responsible` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any comments about any conduct for which the accused was not found not criminally responsible"
    WHEN `form 48.2 a complaint about an individual, other than the accused, involved in the investigation or prosecution` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any complaint about any individual, other than the accused, who was involved in the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
    WHEN `form 48.2 an opinion or recommendation about the disposition` THEN
        IF `the court or the Review Board has approved`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except with the court’s or Review Board’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the disposition": with approval the Form is silent (fork F8)
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except with the court’s or Review Board’s approval, an opinion or recommendation about the disposition"
    WHEN `form 48.2 emotional impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 48.2 physical impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 48.2 economic impact` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 48.2 fears for security` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 48.2 a drawing, poem or letter` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following sections are examples of information you may wish to include in your statement": the sections are examples of information the declarant "may wish to include", and the list of examples is not closed

@ref Form 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) (src:18935)
`form 48.2 this is an application for compensation or restitution` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Please note that this is not an application for compensation or restitution"

@ref Form 48.2 (Subsection 672.5(14)) (src:18915)
`form 48.2 the declarant is required to include all the examples` MEANS JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "You are not required to include all of this information"
